From c19b6a44d01d55661c9eb06823371e4a70f700cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:49:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The Barrows brothers fight properly: styles, set effects,
 prayer drain

Round A of the seven things Corey found. A DAMAGETYPE IS NOT AN AI, which is why Ahrim was walking
up and hitting people with his quarterstaff: param=damagetype tells the engine which of the
player's defences to roll against and nothing else, and every npc here gets melee AI by default -
[ai_queue1,_] sets opplayer2 and [ai_opplayer2,_] swings. A ranged or magic npc needs
~npc_default_retaliate_ap, which sets applayer2, and its own [ai_applayer2] handler; troll
throwers, dark wizards and every fight cave monster were already wired that way. Ahrim and Karil
were not.

Ahrim casts Iban's Blast - the cache has no projectile of his own, and of everything in the spell
table that is the dark purple burst his attack looks like - with the max hit FORCED to the wiki's
20, because off his magic level alone it is 11. One cast in four is Confuse, Weaken or Curse, which
the wiki says he throws and which are real spells here, so the debuffs land through the engine's
own path.

KARIL'S +55 RANGED STRENGTH HAD A HOME AFTER ALL. Part A's comment said this engine has no npc
param for it; param=rangebonus is exactly it, read by ~npc_ranged_maxhit, and 55 through that
formula gives his max hit of 20. It was only ever missing from his record, along with a bolt to
fire - and barrows_karil_tainted_shot turns out to be his SET EFFECT's graphic rather than his
ammunition, so the bolt is the cache's own crossbowbolt_travel.

That correction turned the max hits into a real check. The engine's formula on the bonuses the
infoboxes give: Dharok 29, Guthan 24, Torag 23, Verac 23, Karil 20. All five are the wiki's printed
max hits, out of numbers that were already in the stat blocks - so the bonuses and the max hits
agree through arithmetic neither was copied from. The battery recomputes all six every run.

AND ALL SIX HAVE A SET EFFECT OF THEIR OWN, which the earlier round denied for Dharok in as many
words. Ahrim's Blighted Aura takes 5 Strength on 20% of his hits; Dharok's Wretched Strength adds
one per cent of his max hit for every hitpoint HE is missing, which is 29 at full health and 57 at
one - both the wiki's numbers; Guthan's Infestation heals him for the damage dealt, a quarter of
the time; Karil's Tainted Shot takes a fifth of your Agility; Torag's Corruption takes a fifth of
the run energy you have LEFT; and Verac hits through Protection Prayers a quarter of the time,
which skips the rolls rather than weighting them - "ignoring prayer and armour" means neither is
asked, so a pierced hit lands for 1 to his max and never nothing.

The cache already had the art for the four that need any: barrows_ahirm_blighted_aura (its
spelling), barrows_karil_tainted_shot, barrows_guthan_effect and barrows_torag_effect were four
spotanims nothing in the build was using, which is itself evidence the effects belong to the
brothers rather than to the armour.

Ahrim's and Karil's attacks are ~npc_cast_spell_with_forced_max_hit's and ~npc_rangeattack's own
bodies written out, for one reason: neither reports whether the attack connected and both effects
are "per successful hit". ~npc_player_hit_roll is the roll the spell path makes internally, so
asking it directly is the same roll and not a second one.

THE PRAYER DRAIN: a brother's face every 18 seconds underground for 8 points, plus one per brother
already killed, so the last of them costs 14 - and 8 + 6 is arithmetic rather than a third number.
A player timer started by the dig and by the passage, which takes itself off the moment the player
is anywhere else, and which drains in the crypts AND the tunnels - the same map square two levels
apart. The face is not drawn: barrows_chathead_fade is in the cache for it, but a dialogue that
opens itself every thirty ticks mid-fight is worse than no picture.

Verified: clean build, rs2check 1700 scripts / 490 configs with 0 ERROR and 0 CHECK, all eleven
batteries green, and barrows_battery.py's 586 checks against 148 mutations - each caught by its own
check. One fault worth keeping turned up doing it: a check whose MESSAGE contains the expected
number cannot be identified after a mutation to the spec, because the mutation rewrites the text
the runner matches on.

Still to come: the doors opening instead of carrying you through, the puzzle door, the chest's
reward interface, and the six ARMOUR sets' effects, which are a different six from these.

